        <label>Is Person Account</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Primary_Household_Member</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Person_Account</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Account.IsPersonAccount</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Primary_Member_Person_Account</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Is Person Account</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Determines whether a primary household member was found for the related account. When present, the flow resolves to that person account; otherwise the meeting does not resolve to a person account and no goals can be created or updated.</description>
        <name>Is_Primary_Member_Present</name>
        <label>Is Primary Member Present</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Screen_NoPersonAccount</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Primary Member</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_Primary_Member</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Primary_Household_Member</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>SetPrimaryMemberHousehold</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Is Primary Member Present</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Determines whether any existing goal records were retrieved. Only build the grounding context when there is at least one goal; otherwise call the prompt with an empty context.</description>
        <name>Has_ExistingGoals</name>
        <label>Has Existing Goals</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Assign_EmptyGoalsContext</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Existing_Goals_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Financial_Goals</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsEmpty</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Add_ExistingGoals_Heading</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>false</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
            <isGroupedConditions>false</isGroupedConditions>
            <label>Existing Goals Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>After creating a new goal, only create a completed Task proxy and linking ActionPlanItem when the meeting stage actually has an Action Plan. A financial goal cannot be an ActionPlanItem target, so a completed Task represents the goal on the Meeting Follow-Up Tasks Action Plan. When the stage has no Action Plan, skip this so the flow does not fault on a null master-detail ActionPlanId; the goal is still created and linked to the person account.</description>
        <name>Has_ActionPlan</name>
        <label>Has Action Plan</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_CreateNewGoals</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Action Plan</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Action_Plan_Present</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Meeting_PlaybookStage.ActionPlanId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_Goal_Task</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>false</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
            <isGroupedConditions>false</isGroupedConditions>
            <label>Action Plan Present</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Flow creates and updates financial goals from post-meeting notes for periodic client meetings. Advisors can review AI-suggested new goals and edits to existing goals related to the resolved person account before saving. New goals are linked to the person account via FinServ__PrimaryOwner__c; when the stage has an Action Plan, each created goal is also represented by a completed Task added to the plan. The meeting must resolve to a person account (directly or via a household primary member); otherwise no records are created.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Running user&apos;s display name, built from first + last name. The $User global does not expose a Name/FullName field in Flow formulas, only FirstName/LastName.</description>
        <name>FormulaCurrentUserName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>TRIM({!$User.FirstName} &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; {!$User.LastName})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Subject for the completed Task proxy that represents a created goal on the Action Plan.</description>
        <name>FormulaGoalTaskSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Goal created: &quot; &amp; {!Loop_CreateNewGoals.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Remaps the raw prompt JSON (reviewJson) into the exact key and value forms the industries_common:recordsReviewTable component expects for the FSC FinancialGoal object. The component looks up each cell as record[toEditKey(fieldApiName)], where toEditKey lowercases only the first character of the field API name; so the prompt&apos;s camelCase keys (type, targetAmount, ...) are rewritten to finServ__Type__c, finServ__TargetValue__c, etc. (name already matches). Status picklist values are normalized from the prompt&apos;s screaming-snake enum to the FinServ__Status__c API values (Not Started / In Progress / Completed). Type values are mapped from the base prompt&apos;s fixed 8-value vocabulary (Education, Emergency, Home, Pay off Debt, Retirement, Vacation, Vehicle, Other) to FSC FinServ__Type__c values: Education/Retirement/Other match verbatim; Home becomes Home Purchase; and Emergency, Pay off Debt, Vacation and Vehicle have no FSC equivalent so they fall back to Other. All tokens are matched with their surrounding double quotes so only JSON keys/values are affected, never prose inside a description; the global SUBSTITUTE also covers keys and values inside recordEdits.</description>
        <name>FormulaReviewJsonRemapped</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>SUBSTITUTE(
 SUBSTITUTE(
  SUBSTITUTE(
   SUBSTITUTE(
    SUBSTITUTE(
     SUBSTITUTE(
      SUBSTITUTE(
       SUBSTITUTE(
        SUBSTITUTE(
         SUBSTITUTE(
          SUBSTITUTE(
           SUBSTITUTE(
            SUBSTITUTE(
             {!reviewJson},
             &quot;\&quot;type\&quot;&quot;,         &quot;\&quot;finServ__Type__c\&quot;&quot;),
            &quot;\&quot;targetAmount\&quot;&quot;,  &quot;\&quot;finServ__TargetValue__c\&quot;&quot;),
           &quot;\&quot;targetDate\&quot;&quot;,     &quot;\&quot;finServ__TargetDate__c\&quot;&quot;),
          &quot;\&quot;status\&quot;&quot;,          &quot;\&quot;finServ__Status__c\&quot;&quot;),
         &quot;\&quot;description\&quot;&quot;,      &quot;\&quot;finServ__Description__c\&quot;&quot;),
        &quot;\&quot;NOT_STARTED\&quot;&quot;,       &quot;\&quot;Not Started\&quot;&quot;),
       &quot;\&quot;IN_PROGRESS\&quot;&quot;,        &quot;\&quot;In Progress\&quot;&quot;),
      &quot;\&quot;COMPLETED\&quot;&quot;,           &quot;\&quot;Completed\&quot;&quot;),
     &quot;\&quot;Home\&quot;&quot;,               &quot;\&quot;Home Purchase\&quot;&quot;),
    &quot;\&quot;Emergency\&quot;&quot;,          &quot;\&quot;Other\&quot;&quot;),
   &quot;\&quot;Pay off Debt\&quot;&quot;,       &quot;\&quot;Other\&quot;&quot;),
  &quot;\&quot;Vacation\&quot;&quot;,           &quot;\&quot;Other\&quot;&quot;),
 &quot;\&quot;Vehicle\&quot;&quot;,            &quot;\&quot;Other\&quot;&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Builds the summary message combining the count of new goals created and existing goals updated.</description>
        <name>FormulaSummaryText</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>TEXT({!newCount}) &amp; &quot; goal(s) added, &quot; &amp; TEXT({!updatedCount}) &amp; &quot; goal(s) updated&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Meeting Concierge: Periodic Create New Goals Or Update Existing Goals FSC Package {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <isOverridable>true</isOverridable>
    <label>Meeting Concierge: Periodic Create New Goals Or Update Existing Goals FSC Package</label>
    <loops>
        <description>Iterates over the existing goal records and appends each goal&apos;s details to the grounding context supplied to the review prompt.</description>
        <name>Loop_ExistingGoals</name>
        <label>Loop Existing Goals</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>Get_Financial_Goals</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Add_ExistingGoal_Details</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Call_GoalReviewPrompt</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
    <loops>
        <description>Iterates over each selected new goal returned by the review screen to create the financial goal record and, when the stage has an Action Plan, a completed Task proxy on the plan.</description>
        <name>Loop_CreateNewGoals</name>
        <label>Loop Create New Goals</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>selectedNewRecords</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_New_Goal_Record</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Update_ExistingGoals</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
